        "description_text": "Acer palmatum dissectum 'Irish Lace' Irish Lace Dwarf Weeping Japanese Maple Zones 5-9 ‘Irish Lace’ is a beautiful, yet rare, weeping Japanese maple. The bright cherry-red new growth in the spring matures to a maroon, later developing in a bronze, then a green with bronze highlights for the summer. The cherry red new growth appears again in the summer during the second flush of growth starting this wonderful cycle of colors all over again. In the fall, ‘Irish Lace’ begins as a bright yellow later turning to a bold orange. ‘Irish Lace’ has a mounding and cascading habit similar to other laceleaf Japanese maples reaching 3-4 ft in height by 5-6 ft in width in 10 years. For best color on ‘Irish Lace’ giving morning-mid day sun with protection from the hot afternoon sun. Trees were potted from large liners to gallons in this spring and may not have completely filled out their pots.",
